- description: This metric measures the average time taken to convert a sales lead into a qualified sales opportunity within the sales pipeline. It focuses on the duration from the initial contact with a potential customer to the point where the lead is deemed viable for further sales engagement. By analyzing this cycle time, organizations can identify bottlenecks and inefficiencies in their sales processes, such as delays in lead qualification or inadequate follow-up strategies. The metric provides insights into the effectiveness of sales team activities and the overall health of the sales pipeline. A shorter cycle time typically indicates a more efficient sales process, while a longer cycle time may highlight areas needing improvement.

