Metric:
- id: itsm.case_resolution_time
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the average duration taken to resolve IT service cases within an IT Service Management (ITSM) framework. It focuses on the efficiency and responsiveness of the support team in addressing user-reported issues or service requests. By analyzing the time from case creation to resolution, organizations can identify bottlenecks in their support processes and evaluate the effectiveness of their incident management practices. This metric is crucial for understanding customer satisfaction, as quicker resolution times typically correlate with improved user experiences. Additionally, it helps in resource allocation and workload management by highlighting trends in case resolution performance over time.

