- description: The Incident Reopen Rate measures the percentage of IT service incidents that are reopened after they have been marked as resolved or closed. This metric serves as an indicator of the effectiveness and quality of the incident resolution process within IT Service Management (ITSM). A high reopen rate may suggest that the initial fixes were inadequate or that the underlying issues were not fully addressed, reflecting on the robustness of remediation efforts. It helps organizations identify areas for improvement in their incident management workflows and ensures that service quality meets user expectations. By monitoring this metric, organizations can enhance their problem-solving capabilities and reduce the recurrence of similar incidents.

