Metric:
- id: hr.onboarding_cycle_time
- name: 
- description: The Onboarding Cycle Time metric quantifies the duration required to successfully integrate new employees into the organization. This measurement encompasses all stages of the onboarding process, including HR workflows such as document submission, training sessions, and compliance checks, as well as IT provisioning tasks like account creation and access setup. By analyzing this metric, organizations can identify bottlenecks and inefficiencies within their onboarding processes, allowing for targeted improvements. The scope of this metric includes both administrative tasks handled by HR and technical setups managed by IT, providing a comprehensive view of the onboarding experience. Ultimately, a shorter onboarding cycle time indicates a more efficient and streamlined process, enhancing employee satisfaction and productivity from day one.

