- description: This metric quantifies the time delay between data synchronization events across various integrated systems within an enterprise architecture. It specifically measures the interval from when data is updated in one system to when that update is reflected in another system, highlighting potential inconsistencies in data availability. High latency values may indicate synchronization issues that could lead to discrepancies in reporting, decision-making, and operational efficiency. The scope of this metric encompasses all integrated applications, including ERP, HR, and ITSM systems, ensuring a comprehensive view of data flow across the organization. Monitoring this latency is crucial for maintaining data integrity and supporting timely business processes.

