- description: The Data Quality Exceptions Rate metric measures the frequency at which exceptions are raised by established data quality rules within an ERP, HR, or ITSM system. This metric focuses on identifying recurring issues related to data hygiene and governance, such as inaccuracies, inconsistencies, or missing information in critical datasets. By tracking these exceptions, organizations can pinpoint specific areas where data quality is lacking, enabling targeted interventions to improve overall data integrity. The scope of this metric encompasses all data inputs and outputs that are subject to quality checks, providing a comprehensive view of data governance effectiveness. Ultimately, a high exceptions rate may indicate systemic problems in data management processes that require immediate attention.

