- description: This metric quantifies the technical debt incurred from customizations made to the ERP, HR, or ITSM platforms. It measures the extent to which these customizations deviate from standard configurations, which can complicate future upgrades and reduce system flexibility. By assessing customization debt, organizations can identify potential risks associated with maintaining and evolving their systems. The metric encompasses all types of customizations, including code modifications, workflow alterations, and user interface changes. A high level of customization debt may indicate a need for refactoring or standardization efforts to ensure long-term sustainability and adaptability of the platform.

